// spec: MOD-014
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// modules/BackRef imports this file back.  MOD-014 requires that to work the
// way a cycle between two ordinary modules does [MOD-012], or to be refused by
// name.  It does neither: the root's body runs and prints, and then its OWN
// imported name is undefined.
//
// ⚠️ The root is never entered in the loader's map of loaded files, so BackRef
// parses it a second time and the two copies do not share their names.

uses 'modules/BackRef';

WriteLn ('root body ran');

WriteLn (ModName ());
